├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│         Core Framework                │
│  (Appium, TestNG, etc.)              │
└─────────────────────────────────────┘

Benefits:
- Changes isolated to one layer
- Clear responsibilities
- Easy to extend
- Testers can work at appropriate level
```

**2. Component-Based Architecture**

```
Instead of page objects for whole screens:

LoginScreen (old way)
├── usernameField
├── passwordField
├── loginButton
├── forgotPasswordLink
└── signupLink

Better: Reusable components

InputField component
├── usernameField
└── passwordField

Button component
├── loginButton
├── signupButton
└── submitButton

Navigation component
├── forgotPasswordLink
└── backButton

Benefits:
- Components reused across screens
- Consistent behavior
- Easier maintenance
```

**3. Domain-Driven Test Design**

```java
// Instead of low-level actions:
loginPage.enterUsername("testuser");
loginPage.enterPassword("pass123");
loginPage.clickLogin();

// Use domain language:
user.logsInAs("testuser", "pass123");
user.shouldSeeWelcomeMessage();
user.shouldBeOnDashboard();

// Implementation:
public class User {
    private LoginPage loginPage;
    private DashboardPage dashboardPage;

    public void logsInAs(String username, String password) {
        loginPage.login(username, password);
    }

    public void shouldSeeWelcomeMessage() {
